{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788268013,"nonce":"OLG/AUuvqn7WbmsF8iNwmLE9pHE=","message":"Session 13 live-bench findings, filed as `c718e4a` (site-survey), `3a5ff6c` (dev staging must be able to run the real gate) and `8b4839f` (blocker at the wrong cell). Three consequences for this spec, each verified against the decompiled source on the issues themselves:\n\n1. **Your preflight routine is shared, not yours to write twice.** `c718e4a` defines one routine — `GenConstruct.CanPlaceBlueprintAt(godMode:false)` plus the `Designator_Build.Visible` clauses #3/#4 already owe you — that serves `site-survey`, `find-rect {def}`, `dev:spawn-thing {buildable:true}` and `site-audit`. `build` and `place-layout` preflight CONSUME it. If it does not exist when you start, it is yours to write and theirs to consume — but it is one routine either way, because the acceptance on `c718e4a` asserts that `site-survey`'s verdict and `build`'s refusal for the same arguments are the same sentence.\n\n2. **Instant mode IS `dev:spawn-thing {buildable:true}`, and \"instant ≡ built-blueprint\" is now provable.** #4 said the things-dump diff bullet was untestable. `site-audit` (`3a5ff6c`) re-runs the validator over every player building in a rect: an instant-mode placement that passes the audit is, by construction, a state blueprint mode could have produced. Use that as the bullet instead of an undefined \"modulo construction byproducts\" diff. Instant mode must NOT use the default god-hand path: `GenSpawn.CanSpawnAt` runs no PlaceWorker and, with `canWipeEdifices:true`, `WipeMode.VanishOrMoveAside` erases walls in the footprint without a journal line.\n\n3. **Corner vs centre.** `find-rect`'s `at` is a rect corner; `GenAdj.OccupiedRect(center, rot, size)` places about a centre and, for even sizes, `CellRect.CenterCell` and `OccupiedRect` disagree by one cell. `place-layout --origin P` must say which convention `P` is (the IR's row 0 = north pin makes this concrete) and publish the game's `pos` per placed thing. `c718e4a` publishes `pos` for exactly this reason; the layout verb should hand its per-cell failures back in the same `{at, role, reason, blocker}` shape so a refused layout reads like a refused survey.\n\nThe bench case, for the record: a 3x2 box approved by `find-rect`, refused by the game for granite on the interaction cell one row south — the row a survey of 2–3x the footprint would have shown. That is the acceptance shape Evan wants for siting: **the agent looks at an area 2–3x bigger than whatever it is building.**","files":null}]}